From 6cb4c9c1998e15b0ad9038eaaab426442ac84dfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crindo18 <chrisjohnalado@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 03:27:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] M3 results review: headroom table, per-condition open-set
 reporting

The full baseline run is sound - 27,000 queries in 14.1 min (0.031 s per
query, down from 0.373) and a proper sigmoid across the extended grid.
Two reporting problems, both fixed in s06.

1. Criterion 1 asks for >=10 pp over the baseline at 0 dB. Baseline at
   0 dB is 98.2/99.6/99.9%, so maximum possible gain is 1.8 pp - the
   criterion cannot be met at the SNR it names. There IS room at -5 dB
   (3 s only) and comfortable room at -10 and -15 dB, which is also the
   steepest part of the curve. s06 now prints the headroom per cell so
   this is visible before the enhanced run, not after.

   Recommendation in designNotes: report clean/10/5/0 exactly as the
   proposal specifies, then name -10 dB as the SNR carrying the claim.
   Do not rewrite the criterion after seeing the data.

2. Pooled precision/recall/FAR are grid-composition artefacts, not
   system properties: adding SNR points below the knee mechanically
   lowers pooled recall, and a holdout query at -25 dB is rejected for
   the wrong reason. s06 now reports them per (length, SNR) and labels
   the pooled figure as an artefact.

Verified: system parity holds after the enhancedConfig fix - both tags
now carry n17, and stft/pre/audio/density/bands/hash-packing are
identical between systems. 93 files structurally clean.
